  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a42ff28a-f3cc-429e-978e-a2f4cda681f5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        912,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1520,
        "content": "## AI Receipt Processor\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow lets users send receipt photos or documents to a Telegram bot. Gemini extracts the vendor, amount, date, expense category, payment method, and confidence score.\n\nHigh-confidence expenses are saved directly to Google Sheets. Low-confidence expenses are stored temporarily in an n8n Data Table and the user is asked to confirm or change the category in Telegram.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- Telegram bot credentials\n- Google Gemini credentials\n- Google Sheets credentials\n- an n8n Data Table named `pending_expenses`\n- a Google Sheet for storing expenses\n\n### Setup steps\n\n1. Connect Telegram credentials to the trigger and all Telegram nodes.\n2. Connect Google Gemini credentials to both Gemini nodes and select a Gemini model.\n3. Make a copy of the provided **Expense template** and select it in all three Google Sheets nodes - https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/129ZEubOfaVA1pOjbVCb9GgZQXbC48XTGpH7Zve5hBU0/edit?usp=sharing\n\n4. Map these Google Sheets columns:\n   - `Date`\n   - `Vendor`\n   - `Amount`\n   - `Payment type`\n   - `Expense Category `\n5. Create an n8n Data Table named `pending_expenses` with:\n   - `request_id` \u2014 Number\n   - `resume_url` \u2014 String\n   - `vendor` \u2014 String\n   - `amount` \u2014 Number\n   - `date` \u2014 Date/Time\n   - `category` \u2014 String\n   - `payment_method` \u2014 String\n6. Select this Data Table in all Data Table nodes.\n7. If you are self-hosting n8n, ensure your instance is publicly reachable for Telegram updates and wait/resume URLs.\n8. Activate the workflow and send a receipt photo or document to your Telegram bot.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can customize the confidence threshold, Gemini extraction prompt, expense categories, Telegram messages, Google Sheets columns, and category confirmation buttons.\n\nThe default confidence threshold is `0.65`.\n\nThe default categories are `Food`, `Transport`, `Shopping`, `Services`, and `Other`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
